  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscS&E 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'During a research meeting, scientists discuss a potential drug compound
    that has shown promising results in early lab experiments. The project will be
    reviewed by the Scientific Review Committee next, before animal studies begin.


    <b>What
    does the Scientific Review Committee (SRC) do?</b>'
  explanation: 'The Scientific Review Committee (SRC) evaluates the scientific quality
    and feasibility of a study to ensure it is well designed and justified. Their
    review helps improve the research plan before it moves on to other approval or
    oversight steps. While SRCs do not usually review every early discovery experiment,
    they may review the results and overall study plan to determine whether the science
    is strong enough to move into preclinical animal studies. '
  correctAnswer: Reviews the study plan to ensure the science is strong, appropriate,
    and worth moving forward
  incorrectAnswer1: 'Enforces lab safety rules and provides protective equipment '
  incorrectAnswer2: Monitors patient safety once a new treatment is on the market
  incorrectAnswer3: Reviews and approves the study plan to begin testing a new treatment
    in people
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
